  "Number": 18,
  "Question": "Nine copies of a certain pamphlet cost less than \\(\\$10.00\\) while ten copies of the same pamphlet (at the same price) cost more than \\(\\$11.00.\\) How much does one copy of this pamphlet cost?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$1.07\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$1.08\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$1.09\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$1.10\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$1.11\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Choices A through D all cost at most \\(\\$1.10\\) per copy. At any of those prices, ten copies cost at most\n\\[\n10\\cdot\\$1.10=\\$11.00.\n\\]\nThus none satisfies the requirement that ten copies cost more than \\(\\$11.00\\); equality is not enough.\n\nFor choice E, the two costs are\n\\[\n9\\cdot\\$1.11=\\$9.99<\\$10.00,\n\\]\n\\[\n10\\cdot\\$1.11=\\$11.10>\\$11.00.\n\\]\nBoth conditions hold, so the only listed price that works is \\(\\boxed{\\$1.11}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
